          %title Ribenboim power series
          %h1#ribenboim_power_series Ribenboim power series
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_pages"} Related pages
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong Ribenboim power series
            group (or ring, or field) is a generalization of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
            ring whose exponents can belong to almost any partially ordered
            = succeed "." do
              %em monoid
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                formal Laurent series
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/formal+Laurent+series"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomials"} polynomials
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laurent+polynomials"} Laurent polynomials
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hahn+series"} Hahn series
            as special cases.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            be a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is
            %em artinian
            if it contains no strictly decreasing infinite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain"} chain
            %em narrow
            if it contains no infinite
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antichain"} antichain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %strong Ribenboim power series
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            with coefficients in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(P,A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:P\to A
            whose support
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi supp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≠
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} supp(f) = \{ p\in P \mid f(p)\neq 0 \}
            is artinian and narrow. This is an abelian group under pointwise addition.
          %p
            Now let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            be a strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partially+ordered"} poset
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Pos
                    %mi str
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pos_{str}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            and strict functions (i.e. morphisms that preserve the strict ordering as well as the non-strict one) whose monoidal structure is the cartesian product of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Pos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pos
            (which is not the cartesian product of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Pos
                      %mi str
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pos_{str}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is a monoid and a poset and the multiplication preserves both orders
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \le
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &lt;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt
            on both sides.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is such a “strict pomonoid” and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(M,R)
            is again a ring, with multiplication
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f\cdot g)(m) = \sum_{(m_1,m_2) \in X_m(f,g)} f(m_1)\cdot g(m_2)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_m(f,g)
            is the set of pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi supp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi supp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (m_1,m_2)\in supp(f) \times supp(g)
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_1\cdot m_2 = m
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_m(f,g)
            is always finite.)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=\mathbb{N}
                with the usual order, we obtain the usual ring of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
                with coefficients in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=\mathbb{Z}
                with the usual order, we obtain the usual ring of
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    formal Laurent series
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/formal+Laurent+series"} ?
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=\mathbb{N}
                with the discrete order, we obtain the usual ring of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomials"} polynomials
            %li
              %p
                Similarly, for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
                with the discrete order, we obtain the ring of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laurent+polynomials"} Laurent polynomials
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                is a linearly ordered abelian group and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                a field, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo ,
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(M,R)
                is the field of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hahn+series"} Hahn series
                with value group
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %h2#related_pages Related pages
          %p Other rings of generalized power series include:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Puiseux+series"} Puiseux series
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Novikov+field"} Novikov field
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hahn+series"} Hahn series
          %p
            Hahn series are a special kind of Ribenboim power series, but Puiseux and Novikov series are not. However, they are all instances of the linearization of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finiteness+space"} finiteness space
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BCJS18"} BJCS
